node_modules/
out/
*.vsix
*.zip

# The s7 BINARY the test gate builds for itself, and the full Snd source tree
# tools/build-snd.sh unpacks — 77 MB of somebody else's code, reproducible with
# one command.
#
# The leading slash is load-bearing. Written as a bare `s7` this matches at
# EVERY level, so it also swallowed third-party/s7 — the two source files the
# gate builds the binary FROM, which are committed. Nothing shows it on a
# machine that already has them; a fresh clone loses them and the s7 gate
# fails on a missing file, which is the fault reported one step away from its
# cause.
/s7
/s7.exe
.build/

# bin/ is COMMITTED, deliberately: without it a fresh clone falls back to
# whatever `snd` is on PATH, and on a machine with a Motif build installed
# that means Snd's own X window opening next to the panels. A binary in git is
# a real cost; a surprise GUI on every clone is a worse one.
#
# What is not committed is a build of a platform nobody has tested. Add a
# directory here per platform as it is built, or leave it out.
#
# (No pattern belongs under this paragraph — that is the point of it.)

.vscode-test/
.claude/
